e of long-distance trade." "Ravenna was not, as far as we know, sacked in any of the invasions or wars that beset the Italian peninsular, perhaps testimony to its perceived invulnerability provided by the swamps of the Adriatic coast."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 875, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 798})
